 "text": "Hi, how are you? Try going up and down few times before he gets here, then ignore him climbing. He learns quickly it's easier. Then ask him to imagine he's shopping and picking up your favorite milk at the shop just down hall. Doing errands make it feel less of a challenge. Stick a small weighted bag of rice or sauce beans in front of it, or use a weight box. Whichever you use, mount it just below the level you want to reach. Keep the box on wall, not in box, then open it. Then lift him up rather than going up with him. Once he' comfortable that way, you can pass him down and he' get the idea.",
